{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "PiCrawler — Per-Servo Premotors (12 Premotors, independent joints)",
    "description": "Phase 6.17 architectural experiment.  Splits each bilateral pitch Premotor (which coupled hip2+knee via bilateral_table) into two independent single-output Premotors — one for hip2, one for knee.  Result: 4 hip1 + 4 hip2 + 4 knee = 12 Premotors, each REINFORCE-credited per joint.  Lets the brain explore postures the prior 8-Premotor topology cannot represent (spider stance, asymmetric leg flexion).  Set leg_symmetry_mode=lr_pairs to average pairs at mc_episode_period boundaries.\n\nPhase 6.17b cold-start fix: all 12 Premotors set use_weighted_accel=false (chosen-intent output instead of weighted mean).  Reason: with uniform softmax over symmetric intents [-1,-0.5,0,0.5,1], weighted mean is exactly 0 — body emits zero motion until policy specializes, but it cannot specialize without motion to produce reward.  Chosen-intent mode emits the sampled intent value directly — 4 of 5 intents are non-zero, so the body gets significant random motion from tick 1.  Cost: per-tick output is jumpier (no smoothing across intent uncertainty); slew-limit MAX_SERVO_SPEED bounds the resulting servo motion.",
    "env_target": "picrawler",
    "phase_tag": "v6 phase 6.17b — per-servo + chosen-intent output",
    "derived_from_manifest": true,
    "episode_length": 6000,
    "mc_episode_period": 1500,
    "stability_gain": 0.05,
    "stability_y_norm": 0.5,
    "stability_speed": 0.05,
    "reward_shape": "trapezoid",
    "target_height": 0.085,
    "height_penalty_grace": 0.02,
    "height_penalty_scale": 0.03,
    "height_penalty_gain": 0.05,
    "leg_symmetry": "lr_pairs"
  },
  "version": 1,
  "runtime": {
    "thread_pool": "per_instance",
    "num_threads": 0
  },
  "modules": [
